sentences.l:
She-appeared like-the-full-moon-of completeness in a-night-of good-fortune, * soft-of the-extremities, slender-shaped-of the-stature;
To-her (is) an-eye that-captures mankind with-its-beauty, * and-it-has-imitated the-ruby in the-redness-of the-cheek;
Descends over the-hip the-blackest-of her-hair; * so-beware-of the-snakes from her-hair, the-curly;
And-the-flanks have-softened from-her, and-her-heart * despite its-softness (is) harder than-the-stone, the-hard;
And-she-sends the-arrow-of the-glance from above a-brow * that-hits and-does-not-miss, even-if it-be from a-distance;
When we-embrace and-I-cling-to her-sash, * pushes-me from clasping-her that breast;
So O her-beauty! it-has-surpassed all comeliness; * and O her-stature! you-have-put-to-shame the-branch, the-tender.

And-a-girl whom cleverness has-trained, * you-see the-sun, from her-cheek, borrowed;
She-came in a-shirt of-hers, green, * as veiled the-leaf with-the-pomegranate-blossom;
So-we-said to-her: What (is) the-name-of that garment? * and-she-said: Nay, [mā] fine-one-of the-phrase! —
We-split the-gall-bladders-of a-people with-it, * so-we call-it Splitting-of-the-Gall.

And she-sways between saffron-dyed and-safflower-dyed, * and-ambergris-scented and-musk-scented and-sandal-scented;
Slim-waisted: if says the-youth to-her "Rise," * say her-hips "Sit, and-take-your-time."
And-when she-asked the-union, said her-beauty * "Be-generous," and-said her-coquetry "Do-not-do."
